From 758ca5e9a361d4a1ceeef82c95c33994b575e613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:08:21 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 18f: route extension install and uninstall
 prompts to the host

In embedded mode Chromium's extension install, re-enable and permission confirmations (ShowExtensionInstallDialogImpl: Web Store, CRX, chrome://extensions) and its uninstall confirmation (ExtensionUninstallDialog::Create) become host requests answered with accept or cancel; no Views dialog is created. ExtensionInstallUIDesktop reports install success and failure to the host instead of opening a Browser window, installed bubble or infobar. Extension tabs.create and runtime.openOptionsPage no longer create a Browser window (they fail as with no window). Requests cancel on tab close, profile release and callback replacement; without a callback install prompts abort and uninstall confirmations cancel. ABI 1.32 / bridge 0.34.0 (extension_install_prompts); builds p79-p80, native webstorePrivate cancel/replace/accept through a loopback gallery override, a locally signed CRX dropped on chrome://extensions installing with notification, confirmed uninstall cancel/accept and no Chromium window pass.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
